WEBVTT

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:27.270
<i>The year is 1889.</i>

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:29.730
<i>After countless adventures,
Jean, Nadia and the rest</i>

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:34.110
<i>began a new life on board the Nautilus
as apprentice crewmembers.</i>

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:36.860
<i>Although unaccustomed to
living in a submarine,</i>

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:39.780
<i>they perform their tasks
with enthusiasm.</i>

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:43.080
<i>The Nautilus continues its voyage</i>

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.710
<i>in pursuit of the mysterious
organization, Neo Atlantis.</i>

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.430
Simply amazing, the machines
they have aboard this ship!

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:03.140
Look how fast it cuts through metal!

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:05.180
Look at this, Sanson!

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:07.310
Don't bother me.

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:13.270
Say Hanson, how many days have we
been aboard this ship?

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:17.150
Gosh, it's hard to say, being
inside all the time.

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:19.740
We can only tell by counting how
many meals we've had.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:22.620
That's it! These meals,
I can't stand them!

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:26.830
Breakfast, fish! Lunch, fish!
And fish for supper too!

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:32.340
That's all we have day after day.
Fish, fish, and more fish!

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:36.210
How much longer must we
go on eating fish?

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:39.880
It doesn't bother me. Our Senorita
seems to like it.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:42.430
Miss Electra is awfully kind too.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:48.310
With our Senorita acting like that,
it looks hopeless.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.360
Don't just sit there!
Change into something nice.

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:58.530
But...

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:01.570
I just felt sorry for you.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:06.790
In those baggy clothes, you look awful.

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:09.830
Can't you hurry?!

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:13.500
We'll be late preparing dinner for
my beloved Captain Nemo!

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:15.960
In just a little while, Captain Nemo!

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:21.590
I'm going to fill your stomach
with my love.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:23.850
Come on! Hurry it up!

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:32.100
Please, while it's hot.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:34.730
Today, I've made you
something special.

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:37.230
Thank you.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.690
Thanks for the food!

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:47.370
How do you like it?

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:49.870
It's delicious.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:53.250
I'm so delighted!

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:02.380
You must eat too, King.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:16.060
How do I look? This is one of Grandis'
dresses cut to my size.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:22.150
You look pretty, Nadia!

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:23.860
Thank you.

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:27.580
What do you think, Jean?

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:32.580
Oh, thanks.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.460
Jean!

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:42.970
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:47.300
I know my manners are terrible.
Marie is always scolding me.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:52.310
So, you were visiting
Miss Electra again.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.480
I don't care!

00:04:56.350 --> 00:05:00.360
What is she so mad about?
Women are hard to figure out.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:01.940
Stupid.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:10.790
I can't take it anymore!

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.540
I can't stand this any longer!

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.540
Day after day, we have nothing
but fish, fish and more fish!

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:20.000
I hate the sight of fish!

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.960
It's not just the fish I'm
sick and tired of!

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:27.680
What good is my new suit if I have to
stay inside this ship every day?

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:30.930
A big, juicy beef steak now
and then would be...

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:33.680
That's enough! Where do you expect
me to find a steak like that?!

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:36.350
I'm trying so hard with the little
stock we have on board.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:37.980
Now, now, Senorita.

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:43.360
You have all been living on land till
now, being unhappy is natural,

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:48.110
but it's only until you get
used to this life.

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:50.580
It's just as the chief cook says.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:56.080
As long as you stay with us, you must
get used to our way of life.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:59.080
I'm perfectly satisfied with this life.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:02.130
I don't mind having fish every
day, Miss Electra.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:06.920
I'm sorry to have the same menu every
day, but please bear with us.

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:10.340
Wait a minute! Just what do
you mean by that?!

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:13.760
You have any complaints
with my cooking?!

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:16.890
Did I say something wrong?

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:26.530
Captain Nemo!

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:30.410
Have you finished?

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:34.240
Excuse me.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:40.170
You haven't finished your dessert yet!

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:42.880
No, thank you.

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:58.310
He didn't eat my dessert.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:04.190
Sanson, it's all your fault for
talking out of turn!

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:08.150
But I just said what I honestly felt.

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:11.110
Quiet! If you hate fish so much,

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:13.120
then eat this!

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:18.370
Stop it! Both of you!

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:21.250
You keep out of this! Wait, Sanson!

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:26.090
Stop! All of you!

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.260
Everyone certainly has bad manners!

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:37.560
Are you worried?

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:40.520
No, not me.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:43.230
I mean our guests.

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:48.190
I don't think they're used to
life on board as yet.

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:54.450
I know. If we don't have any contact
with the Garfish today,

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:57.580
we'll declare tomorrow our day
for hunting. I'll go too.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:59.330
I understand.

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:06.340
Is something the matter?

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.670
No, it's nothing.

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:21.350
An island?! Does that mean we're
going to go ashore someplace?

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:22.690
That's right.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:24.520
All right!

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:38.120
Both engines off.
We'll tie up the Nautilus.

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:43.210
Anchor down.

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:46.170
The ship is secured!

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:49.710
Roger. Everyone, get ready
to go ashore!

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:54.510
Today I'm going to eat
nothing but meat!

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:56.970
Shucks, Miss Electra isn't coming.

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:01.270
They're leaving already!

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:02.890
Come on, Nadia, let's hurry!

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:08.110
I thought Jean would prefer to be with
Miss Electra reading a book.

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:10.570
That's not so.

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:13.070
We're not sure, are we, King?

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:17.870
Okay, let's go!

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:24.160
I never knew there were so
many people on board.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:26.620
Really, we never see them normally.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:30.420
Seeing them like this, we can tell that
they come from many countries.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:34.470
Yes, blacks and whites working in
harmony. It's hard to believe.

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:39.350
You can think of this ship
as a sort of utopia.

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:41.310
Captain Nemo!

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:45.520
Every human being has a different
way of looking at things.

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:47.600
That's why it's so hard for people

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:51.440
to be tolerant of other people,
and live in equality.

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:55.360
But the people on our
ship are different.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:58.410
We are together to achieve
a common goal.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:00.370
A common goal?

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:03.290
That's right, to destroy Neo Atlantis!

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:07.870
I think I've said too much.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:13.300
Well, shall we go ashore too?

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:15.260
Yes, Sir!

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:36.240
How about a little help, Senorita?

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:38.860
I wasn't brought up to do menial tasks.

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:42.240
Why I've never held anything heavier
than a knife and fork.

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:47.870
It can't be...

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:53.960
It's him! Captain Nemo!

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:57.460
Captain Nemo is coming!
What should I do?!

00:10:57.460 --> 00:11:03.470
Maybe this evening we can walk
together alone on the beach?

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:06.390
I've got to hurry and get
ready to meet him!

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:09.440
Nothing's more fearful than
a woman in love.

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:12.350
I hope Miss Electra is coming too.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:20.860
Young people today have no modesty!

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:24.120
They say there's nothing more
fearful than a girl in love.

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:29.160
Even our captain must feel happy to
have a woman fawning over him.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:35.090
Well, her language may be coarse at
times, but she is good looking,

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:37.170
and she also has a nice figure.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:40.260
Her cooking is quite professional too.

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:42.300
Yes, quite tasty, if you
overlook its looks.

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:50.140
If I were ten years, no, twenty years
younger, I'd go after her!

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:56.520
The captain went ashore too.
That shows he has some interest.

00:11:56.520 --> 00:12:00.110
Could be. Now that would
be interesting.

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:03.030
I'm going ashore too.

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:05.240
I leave the ship in your hands!

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:14.120
She looked fearsome, but she went.

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:19.420
Yeah. It'll do her good to forget about
Neo Atlantis for a while.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:26.640
She must be more honest with her
feelings, like Senorita Grandis.

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:32.940
If Captain Nemo has arrived,
it's time to use this.

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:35.690
Captain Nemo won't be
able to resist this.

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:41.900
Under starlit skies, walking along the
beach our romance will blossom!

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:45.860
Now, I must hustle! Hustle!

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:02.050
Say, what are you doing?

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:06.590
Go away! This is no place for a kid.

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:28.120
Well...

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:40.460
Sanson, how dare you?!

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:53.810
I don't believe it. It hit him!

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:55.020
That was pretty good!

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:04.780
Just a bit more, King.

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:08.700
Everyone, may I have your
attention please?

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:25.090
Where is Captain Nemo?

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:30.430
I don't know. I haven't seen him.

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:38.440
Senorita Grandis, the captain has gone
off on a survey of the island.

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:42.020
I thought you were supposed
to remain on board.

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:44.610
Sorry, there was some business
to look after.

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:50.030
How disappointing! I wanted to show
him my bathing suit so much.

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:55.540
I'd think of my age if I were you.
You'll catch cold in that.

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:57.290
What was that?!

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:01.540
You shut up! How old do you think
I am?! I'm still in my twenties!

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:05.050
Yes, but on the wrong side.

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:08.800
That's none of your business!
What about you?!

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:12.300
I'll be reaching twenty in a while.

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:16.060
Sure. Maybe they count differently
where you're from!

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:18.810
What did you say?!

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:27.940
Shall we go and look at the ocean?

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:36.740
The sand can be quite hot on our feet.

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:41.370
I never knew walking on sand
could be so delightful.

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:44.880
We've only the steel floor of the
submarine to walk on.

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:47.840
Jean, look at how pretty
the shells are!

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.970
They sure are pretty!

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:13.530
What a gorgeous view!

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:21.750
If my heart were a seagull
sailing on the winds,

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:26.460
Captain Nemo, then you would
truly be the ocean.

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:34.970
Senorita Grandis, there is something
I must say to you.

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:36.550
Yes?!

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:41.230
Captain Nemo, I've brought you
the data file on the island.

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:45.230
Oh, I'm sorry if I'm interrupting.

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:46.980
You certainly are!

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:49.730
Captain Nemo, you were about to say?

00:16:49.730 --> 00:16:52.030
We'll talk again later.

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:53.700
Let me see that data.

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:57.370
Yes, Sir. I'll be returning
to the Nautilus.

00:16:57.370 --> 00:17:00.910
One of us should be on
board at all times.

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:04.210
Oh yes, Senorita?

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:05.540
Yes?

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:10.550
You'd better change into something
warmer. You'll catch cold in that.

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:23.350
Here we go! Today,

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:26.690
we're going to eat meat, meat,
meat and more meat!

00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:29.480
I can't wait! Let's get going!

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:32.480
Come back safely!

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:34.740
We'll bring back food!

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:36.110
Okay!

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:38.120
Where are Jean and the others going?

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:39.530
Hunting!

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:41.080
Hunting?

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:58.640
Now, we just wait for it to cook.

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:02.390
Miss Grandis, you're so
womanly and gentle.

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:06.390
You should know I was brought
up in a good home.

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:09.520
You should learn more about
home-making, not just acrobatics.

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:11.860
I'm just ignorant.

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:17.650
It brings back memories of when I
was called Mademoiselle.

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:26.540
I was born the only daughter of the
Granba family, wealthy mine owners.

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:35.170
Mama was sickly, and she
died when I was small,

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:38.880
leaving behind happy memories
and jewels.

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:43.470
Then I became the center
of Papa's world.

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:46.480
How he pampered me.

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:48.890
It was one happy day after another.

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:58.900
And then I grew up.

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:02.450
I was sixteen, and it was my first
dance party. That evening,

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:05.910
I met a handsome young man,

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:10.370
a dignified gentleman from
a noble family.

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:13.210
We fell in love right away.

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:16.340
We got engaged against Papa's wishes.

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:22.050
And then what happened?

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:27.140
Papa was right.

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:30.600
That man was nothing,
but a swindler.

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:33.060
His being a nobleman
was a complete lie.

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:37.110
He only approached me to get
his hands on Papa's money.

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:42.610
Papa became his guarantor, and was
forced to back his huge debts.

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:47.330
He was an out and out crook. I was
not only betrayed by my first love,

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:50.040
but I lost my home too.

00:19:59.090 --> 00:20:00.880
And then what happened?

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:08.430
All the people who used to fuss
over me went away.

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:12.850
The only ones left were
Sanson, Hanson,

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:16.690
and the jewelry box that Mama left.

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:21.990
What saved us in the end were the
jewels that Mama left for me.

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:25.160
All those jewels changed
into none for us.

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:30.450
I was so grateful.
They never betrayed me.

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:35.130
From that time on, I made up my mind
that I'd live only for jewels.

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:38.590
I was going to possess all
the jewels in the world.

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:46.180
Don't worry. I don't want your
Blue Water anymore.

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:46.760
Why not?

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:49.470
I found another reason to live.

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:55.310
Captain Nemo, he's a jewel of the
seas, a man among men!

00:20:56.860 --> 00:21:02.070
The Blue Water may be precious to
you, but Jean is more precious.

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:06.820
Can't you see how much
he cares for you?

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:08.950
You should treat him more preciously.

00:21:09.240 --> 00:21:11.040
Jean is only a friend!

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:14.080
Right now he may be just a friend,

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:17.000
but in time, you will begin to
feel grateful toward him.

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:19.840
No one can live alone.

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:24.550
Who's there?!

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:36.560
We're back!

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:40.520
Oh, it's just you. You gave us a scare!

00:21:40.520 --> 00:21:43.690
Look! We had a good hunt!

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:46.320
I see! Welcome back!

00:21:47.070 --> 00:21:49.030
Look! It's meat!

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:56.290
Can't you show more delicacy?

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:02.630
You should learn a little
from Captain Nemo.

00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:08.090
Sanson was terrific! He brought
it down with a single shot.

00:22:08.090 --> 00:22:10.850
Naturally, I'm a genius with a gun.

00:22:11.220 --> 00:22:14.100
Well, shall we have deer
steak for dinner?

00:22:15.060 --> 00:22:16.890
You killed it!

00:22:19.060 --> 00:22:20.610
It's only a baby.

00:22:20.810 --> 00:22:23.440
Don't you feel sorry for what you did?!

00:22:26.320 --> 00:22:29.070
I hate you! I hate you!
I hate all of you!

00:22:29.610 --> 00:22:31.070
Nadia!

00:22:34.620 --> 00:22:36.120
What is she so mad about?

00:22:36.120 --> 00:22:38.750
I don't understand girls.

00:22:46.210 --> 00:22:49.970
Nobody... Nobody seems to understand
what I'm saying.

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:55.600
No! Stay away from me! Go away!

00:22:56.600 --> 00:23:01.100
I've been living on my own until now!
I can keep on living alone!

00:23:12.780 --> 00:23:14.780
I'm sorry! Forgive me, King!

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:20.750
Actually, I'm so lonely.

00:23:38.140 --> 00:23:40.730
What can it be? I feel
something dreadful.
